<Layout title="Community Moderation Policy — Don't Lose Your Way" description="How Don’t Lose Your Way moderates anonymous community submissions to maintain a safe, supportive environment.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <p>Effective Date: May 12, 2026</p>
      <p>This policy describes how Don't Lose Your Way moderates anonymous community submissions to maintain a safe, supportive environment.</p>
      <h1>What We Moderate</h1>
      <p>We moderate all community voice submissions before they are published on the platform. This includes any anonymous reflections, stories, or messages submitted through the community features.</p>
      <h2>Content That Will Not Be Published</h2>
      <p>The following types of content will not be published:</p>
      <h3>Crisis-Related Content</h3>
      <ul>
      <li>Explicit expressions of intent to harm oneself or others</li>
      <li>Descriptions of suicide methods or self-harm instructions</li>
      <li>Content that could encourage or trigger self-harm in others</li>
      </ul>
      <p>*Instead of publishing this content, we display a message directing users to crisis resources (988 Lifeline, Crisis Text Line).*</p>
      <ul>
      <li><strong>Hate speech or discrimination:</strong> Content targeting any group based on race, ethnicity, gender, sexual orientation, disability, religion, or other protected characteristics</li>
      <li><strong>Harassment or bullying:</strong> Content that attacks, threatens, or intimidates individuals or groups</li>
      <li><strong>Personal information:</strong> Content containing names, phone numbers, addresses, emails, or other identifying information</li>
      <li><strong>Promoting violence:</strong> Content that encourages or glorifies violence</li>
      <li><strong>Illegal content:</strong> Content that promotes illegal activities</li>
      <li><strong>Spam or advertising:</strong> Commercial content or repetitive submissions</li>
      <li><strong>Medical advice:</strong> Content that provides specific medical or psychiatric advice to others</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Content That Is Welcome</h2>
      <p>We encourage submissions that are:</p>
      <ul>
      <li>Personal reflections and experiences with mental health challenges</li>
      <li>Messages of hope, resilience, and encouragement</li>
      <li>Honest stories about difficult times and how you got through them</li>
      <li>Creative expressions — poetry, short thoughts, affirmations</li>
      <li>Sharing what helps you cope, stay grounded, or find your way</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Moderation Process</h2>
      <ul>
      <li><strong>All submissions are reviewed before publication.</strong> Nothing is published automatically</li>
      <li>Review happens within a reasonable timeframe — this is not instantaneous</li>
      <li>Submissions may be edited for clarity or to remove identifying information before publication</li>
      <li>Submissions that do not meet our guidelines are not published</li>
      <li>We cannot provide individual feedback on why a submission was not published</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Privacy &amp; Anonymity</h2>
      <ul>
      <li>Community voice submissions are anonymous by default — we do not collect names or contact information</li>
      <li>Do not include personal identifying information in your submission (yours or anyone else's)</li>
      <li>We may track IP addresses for safety and moderation purposes, but these are never displayed publicly</li>
      <li>We cannot contact individual submitters — submissions are anonymous</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Enforcement</h2>
      <p>If a user repeatedly submits content that violates this policy:</p>
      <ul>
      <li>We may restrict or block access from the associated IP address</li>
      <li>We may temporarily or permanently disable submission features for problematic sources</li>
      <li>We report content involving imminent harm to appropriate authorities when possible and required by law</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Reporting Concerns</h2>
      <p>If you see published content that concerns you or violates this policy, please contact us at safety@cc3po.com.</p>
      <p>If you or someone you know is in crisis:</p>
      <ul>
      <li><strong>Call or text 988</strong> — U.S. Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline</li>
      <li><strong>Text TALK to 741741</strong> — Crisis Text Line</li>
      <li><strong>Call 911</strong> — For emergencies</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
      <p>We may update this policy periodically. Changes will be noted on this page.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
